78	@@ -115,20 +115,28 @@ Example with ATE's default numbers: one full planter block of 64 nickel seeds wi
79	 ## Server config
80	 
81	 | Option | Default | Meaning |
82	 |---|---|---|
83	 | `part_cap` | 24 | Most parts in one multiblock, not counting the core |
84	 | `power_block_buffer` | 4,000,000 | RF each power block holds |
85	 | `me_interval` | 20 | Ticks between ME item moves and fertilizer top-ups (1 to 1200) |
86	 
87	 ATE's numbers are never copied into this config. They are read from ATE.
88	 
89	+## Jade
90	+
91	+With Jade installed, looking at a core shows "Formed: N / cap parts" or "Not formed: <problem>". Looking at a planter block shows its status and how many of its seeds are growing, as "growing/total seeds growing". Both can be turned off in Jade's plugin settings.
92	+
93	+## Guide
94	+
95	+The in-game guide is an Oracle Index book. Its pages live in `wiki/` and `processResources` copies them into the jar. Oracle Index is optional and this mod has no code for it.
96	+
97	 ## Build
98	 
99	 ```
100	 ./gradlew build
101	 ```
102	 
103	 The jar is `build/libs/modular_planters-0.1.0.jar`. `./gradlew runGameTestServer` runs the in-game tests.
104	 
105	 ## License
