994	@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
995	+---
996	+title: Building Rules
997	+---
998	+
999	+- The multiblock is the core plus every part connected to it face to face, directly or through other parts. Diagonal contact does not connect.
1000	+- It needs at least one power block, one export block and one planter block. Fertilizer and frame blocks are optional.
1001	+- At most 24 parts, not counting the core. Frames count. The cap is in the server config.
1002	+- If the connected parts reach a second core, neither core forms. The core screen names the problem block and its position.
1003	+- When the shape breaks, planter blocks stop and every block keeps its contents.
1004	+
1005	+<Callout variant="info">
1006	+If a connected part is in an unloaded chunk, the multiblock pauses until the chunk loads, and the core screen says so.
1007	+</Callout>
1008	+
1009	+<Callout variant="info">
1010	+The core can't tell what is in an unloaded chunk, so a multiblock built against the edge of the loaded area also pauses until the next chunk loads, even when no part is in it.
1011	+</Callout>
