1059	--- /dev/null
1060	+++ b/wiki/docs/growing.mdx
1061	@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
1062	+---
1063	+title: How a Planter Block Grows
1064	+---
1065	+
1066	+- Growing seeds G is the smaller of the seed count and the soil count. Seeds past that stay idle.
1067	+- One module covers one seed. Module 1 covers the first seeds in the bin and module 2 does the same, so seeds fill both modules first.
1068	+- Seeds with the same modules and the same seed data grow as a group. Each seed levels on its own, as it would in its own Powered Planter.
1069	+- Growth time, power and fertilizer follow ATE's formulas and are read from ATE's live config. Power is drawn each tick for every seed that is still growing. If the power blocks can't cover a planter block's full draw, its seeds stop growing for that tick. Seeds that are already ready still harvest.
1070	+- Fertilizer is taken from the first non-empty slot of the fertilizer blocks. Each tick, planter blocks claim it in position order, and each group claims one item for every one of its seeds or nothing. A group without a claim grows and harvests unfertilized that tick. A claim uses up fertilizer only when its group harvests, so the fertilizer stored speeds up only as many seeds as it can pay for. A paused group keeps claiming each tick, the way a paused Powered Planter keeps its own fertilizer, so planter blocks later in the order can run unfertilized while it waits.
1071	+- When there is no room in the export blocks, planter blocks wait. Nothing is voided.
1072	+- Breaking a block drops everything it holds.
1073	+- Picking up the whole seed run and putting it back, or scrolling seeds out and back in one at a time, restarts those seeds' growth. No items are lost.
1074	+
1075	+See [planter](@modular_planters:planter) for the block itself.
1076	diff --git a/wiki/docs/logistics_networks.mdx b/wiki/docs/logistics_networks.mdx
1077	new file mode 100644
1078	index 0000000..62196a0
1079	--- /dev/null
1080	+++ b/wiki/docs/logistics_networks.mdx
1081	@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
1082	+---
1083	+title: Logistics Networks
1084	+---
1085	+
1086	+Logistics Networks is optional and this mod has no code for it. A node on the core works through the core's connections. The node needs an upgrade sized to the multiblock. A node uses its best upgrade for every channel, and these are Logistics Networks' default limits:
1087	+
1088	+| Node upgrade | Energy per tick | Items a second |
1089	+|---|---|---|
1090	+| None | 2,000 RF | 0.8 |
1091	+| Iron | 10,000 RF | 64 |
1092	+| Gold | 50,000 RF | 256 |
1093	+| Diamond | 250,000 RF | 5,120 |
1094	+| Netherite | about 2.1 billion RF | 200,000 |
1095	+
1096	+Example with ATE's default numbers: one full planter block of 64 nickel seeds with 2 MK3 Speed Modules, insanium farmland and the built-in cloche.
1097	+
1098	+- Power: it draws 32,768 RF/t whatever the seeds' traits.
1099	+- Items: with seeds that have no traits it puts out about 24 items a second. With seeds maxed in Productive Farming's Growth and Yield it puts out about 320 items a second, which is more than a gold upgrade moves.
1100	+- Upgrade needed: a diamond upgrade covers up to 7 such planter blocks, and power is the limit. More than 7 needs a netherite upgrade, or more nodes on the power blocks.
1101	diff --git a/wiki/docs/overview.mdx b/wiki/docs/overview.mdx
1102	new file mode 100644
1103	index 0000000..96191c4
1104	--- /dev/null
1105	+++ b/wiki/docs/overview.mdx
1106	@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
1107	+---
1108	+title: Modular Planters
1109	+---
1110	+
1111	+Modular Planters is a NeoForge addon for Agritech: Evolved (ATE) that replaces many Powered Planters with a few multiblocks. A planter block with N growing seeds produces and draws what N Powered Planters would, and one connection to the core runs the whole multiblock.
1112	+
1113	+It needs ATE 2.2.0 or newer. An optional ME block connects a multiblock to an AE2 network, with Applied Flux support. It needs AE2 and does not exist without it.
1114	+
1115	+## Blocks
1116	+
1117	+| Block | Job |
1118	+|---|---|
1119	+| Core | Forms the multiblock, applies the built-in cloche, opens the core screen, and is the doorway for energy, fertilizer and outputs. It stores nothing itself. |
1120	+| Power | Stores energy. Several power blocks pool their storage. Energy goes in but can't be taken out. A broken power block keeps its energy in the dropped item. |
1121	+| Fertilizer | 27 slots shared by every planter block. It accepts only ATE fertilizers. |
1122	+| Export | 54 slots that hold outputs until something pulls them out. Only the multiblock can insert. Anything can extract. |
1123	+| Planter | Grows one seed type, up to 64 seeds. It has a seed slot, a soil slot and two module slots. |
1124	+| Frame | Connects parts and does nothing else. |
1125	+| ME | Connects the multiblock to an AE2 network. It exists only when AE2 is installed. |
1126	+
1127	+Fertilizer and export blocks drop their contents when broken.
